Z||000000||oneof547||02-08-2001||11:40 PM||||Just another quick question.......<BR>I have an 88 formula: last year i replaced the rear bushings with prothane bushings,(i highly recomend them) not a single noise or squeek out of them since installing. About a month ago while having new tires and allignment done i let the local tire place install the front bushings (big mistake).They squeek almost on every bump in the road.  Is there a way to fix this disaster without re-doing or replacing the entire job?? what about installing grease fittings into the control arms themselves. Unfortunatley the shop will not stand behind thier work regarding the noise.<P>------------------<BR>oneof547<p>[This message has been edited by oneof547 (edited 02-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||02-09-2001||10:22 AM||||i'm not sure if you can install zerk fittings with the control arms on the car..  it fyou could that would help but you still wont get the STOOOPID gooey grease that comes with the kit in the cent hole (the real pivit point..  sorry.. i'd say disassemble and lube it with the psycho grease that they came with and have it re-aligned||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||02-09-2001||12:30 PM||||disassemble and regrease.  thats what i did on the left front... quite as a mouse, now.<P>i still need to do the right front.<P>and don't forget to remove and grease the inner sleaves as well!  thats where a lot of the problem comes from.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
